<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adnan Menderes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1899">1899</a>–<a href="/years/1961">1961</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adnan Menderes was a Turkish politician who co-founded the Democrat Party and became prime minister after its victory in the 1950 election, the first peaceful transfer of power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republic-of-turkey">Turkish Republic</a>. His government encouraged private enterprise and agriculture, brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> in 1952 and relaxed some secularist restrictions. Overthrown by the military coup of 1960, he was tried and hanged in 1961.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adnan-menderes.jpg" alt="Adnan Menderes" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adnan_Menderes_VI._Yasama_D%C3%B6nemi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
